            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Does meta not have to support N-1 testing or rolling back updates?\nBecause now we're already broken, as we know that the old code doesn't support the .json files being in the same directory as the cereal files.\n\nIBM happens to be at a breakpoint right now where I think we're safe from this, but in general it's standard practice to go from old to new and back again all the time.  It seems like that would also be standard practice for others selling and testing servers, though I don't know.\n\nI'm not really sure what to do though, either possibly break people, or move the JSON files into a new directory."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "@geissonator@yahoo.com Would this cause problems for the rainier CI that runs?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Right now we're only doing sim testing for these upstream commits, so that's a fresh sim session every time (no persistent files)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "We should move the JSON into a new directory to support backwards compatibility.  I missed that.\n\n> Does meta not have to support N-1 testing or rolling back updates?\n\nGenerally we do not downgrade or require backwards compatibility.  We only move forward.\n\n> IBM happens to be at a breakpoint right now where I think we're safe from this, but in general it's standard practice to go from old to new and back again all the time.\n\nYes, I think this is reasonable to have to support."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Yea, I missed it too, it probably should have gone in with the commit that introduced this file.\n\nSo I think if we do that then these 3 commits won't be needed.\n\n@architmehrotra@meta.com maybe you can add a json subdir for your new file?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> So I think if we do that then these 3 commits won't be needed.\n\nWe definitely still need some or all of these 3 commits even if I move it.  But I'll try to simplify what can be simplified if a simple move makes it not necessary."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 712,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Even easier is:\n\nif (id.ends_with(json))\n    continue\n\nWhat advantage is the current method?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 712,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I think Archit was planning on adding support to deserialize from JSON as well.  That way we can make a transition from Cereal to JSON.  Continuing to add the ID into the map makes it easier to deal with that code below in the near future.\n\n(Maybe I'll add it quickly)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "log_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 712,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Ack"
                }
            ],
